.TH MW-MCP 1 "2026-07-03" "MemoryWhale" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server over MemoryWhale memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-mcp
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets an AI agent query your
MemoryWhale memory directly, instead of pasting it in. It speaks
newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 on standard input and output and takes no
arguments. It reads the same local database as the rest of the CLI and honours
.BR MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR .
.PP
Register it once with an MCP client, e.g. Claude Code:
.PP
.RS
.B claude mcp add memorywhale -- mw-mcp
.RE
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B recent_errors
Recent failed commands (non-zero exit) with their error output.
.TP
.B search_memory
Search remembered commands, arguments, output, and notes for a term.
.TP
.B get_context
A compact digest of recent failures, optionally scoped to a project tag.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR
Override the data directory (default
.IR <data_local>/MemoryWhale ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-serve (1)
